& [SJS]
  + Situation: Slice2 now produces an exact proof-bearing catalogue but no bounded operator turns query terms and known identities into gated SemanticAddress candidates
  + Justification: exact provider-free scanning is the highest-leverage path from signed SOP fabric to later attention loading and can be implemented without lexical or model inference
  + Solution: add one deterministic scanner that validates roots gathers exact channels applies non-inventive gates traverses allowed typed relations orders by PriorityLattice and returns proof-bound candidates with honest clipping

& [CompletedWorkSupportReview]
  + [completed_slice_id] Slice2DeterministicFabricDerivation
  + [proof_ref] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_Semantic_Anchor_Catalogue_P0_Slice2_Proof.sop
  + [support_delta] exact identity entries labels relation adjacency source anchors generation roots and full canonical rebuild validation are verified and current
  + [support_delta] AnchorQuery AnchorCandidate AnchorQueryResult PriorityTier contributions budgets boundary account proof continuation and digest forms are stable from Slice1
  + [requirement_delta] derived use_cases included_boundaries excluded_boundaries protected_identities operation_entries and applicability_bindings are currently absent unless future admitted structure supplies them
  + [requirement_delta] AuthorityContext exposes allowed package scopes operation and effect boundary while package certificates expose projects namespaces semantic kinds perspectives and capabilities
  + [support_gap] no scanner currently binds those forms into exact staged behavior
  + [readiness_recompute] Slice3 is ready if absent declarations become unresolved guards or omissions and only exact currently represented facts decide admission

& [Delineation]
  + exact known identity and compiled exact-label equality are inside
  + purpose lifecycle read-scope and declared boundary gating are inside
  + declared applicability is inside only for exact structured bindings already present in the validated catalogue
  + typed relation traversal is inside only for relation identities and types already present in the matching admitted fabric
  + lexical similarity embeddings learned routes provider prompts semantic paraphrase and inferred applicability are outside
  + candidate relevance never becomes authority permission truth confidence risk or safety arithmetic
  + an absent gate declaration is unresolved evidence not proof of incompatibility
  + catalogue and scan results remain disposable projections while admitted packages remain authority

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [conceptual_model] query exact seed gate disposition contribution relation path candidate lattice boundary account proof continuation
  + [logical_model] validate roots then gather exact identity then exact label then gate then applicability then relation then lattice then exact resolve then clip and commit
  + [physical_model] dependency-light pure Rust BTree maps sets vectors and canonical serde JSON digest commitments
  + [source_data] AnchorQuery DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue SemanticFabric IdentityAnchorEntry ApplicabilityBinding SemanticRelation package certificate and SourceAnchor
  + [derived_projection] AnchorQueryResult with candidate contributions record identities source anchors boundary account proof continuation and result digest
  + [freshness_rule] any request catalogue fabric candidate address or cursor identity change invalidates the output or continuation
  + [recompute_rule] rerun from the same immutable inputs and never patch candidate ranks proof or cursor
  + [authoritative_store] admitted packages
  + [derived_store] returned in-memory scan value only

& [OperatorContract]
  + [input] validated DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue matching SemanticFabric valid AnchorQuery and optional prior scanner cursor
  + [output] deterministic AnchorQueryResult containing only exact-channel candidates and proof
  + [precondition] query permits only Slice3 channels effect boundary is read_only and catalogue canonical rebuild equals the fabric
  + [postcondition] every address-bearing candidate exact-resolves to the same derived entry admitted unit package and source anchors
  + [failure_behavior] return one typed AnchorScanFault without partial uncommitted output
  + [side_effect] none

& [FeatureRequirementSupport]
  + [SAC3-001] validate query derived catalogue matching fabric and allowed exact channels before scanning; support prepared by current validators and new typed scan fault
  + [SAC3-002] gather exact identity and exact label with inspectable bases and stable deduplication; support prepared by known_identities and exact_label_index
  + [SAC3-003] apply lifecycle authority purpose use-case and boundary gates without invented facts; support prepared with explicit dispositions unresolved guards and omissions
  + [SAC3-004] join declared applicability only when exact bindings and guards exist; support prepared by closed binding forms though current derived fabric truthfully yields none
  + [SAC3-005] traverse allowed typed relations under cycle depth and path bounds; support prepared by fabric relation identities and catalogue adjacency
  + [SAC3-006] enforce PriorityLattice stable ranks winning ambiguity and exact resolution; support gap is scanner implementation and adversarial proof
  + [SAC3-007] clip deterministically under candidate record path byte and continuation budgets with root-bound cursor; support gap is cursor codec and pagination proof
  + [SAC3-008] preserve rollback external boundaries and full workspace compatibility; support prepared by additive pure API and regression gates
  + [slice_readiness] ready_after_phase_lock

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + Master view: the scanner is a lens over the semantic field that keeps candidate relationships purposes and absences visible together
  + Emissary view: exact indexes explicit gate predicates bounded breadth-first traversal lattice tuples and committed cursors make the lens reproducible
  + correction: treating an empty derived boundary or use-case set as permissive would hide missing contract structure while treating it as mismatch would invent exclusion
  + reconciliation: absence becomes an unresolved guard or omission and only represented admitted evidence grants a positive gate conclusion

& [Premortem]
  + failure: label ambiguity collapses arbitrarily; cause first-match lookup; mitigation gather all exact IDs and mark winning ties ambiguous
  + failure: relevance bypasses authority; cause traversal before gates; mitigation lifecycle authority purpose and boundary gates precede relation expansion
  + failure: absent operation fields act as permission; cause empty-set permissiveness; mitigation declared applicability emits nothing without exact bindings and records omission
  + failure: relation walk escapes budgets or cycles; cause unbounded graph expansion; mitigation allowed types visited-depth map deterministic queue and path count clipping
  + failure: continuation resumes changed meaning; cause cursor lacks roots or request digest; mitigation commit roots input digest offset and ordinal into verified opaque cursor
  + failure: byte budget lies; cause clipping before serialization; mitigation serialize candidate result deterministically and reduce tail until within budget or return typed insufficiency
  + failure: Slice3 accidentally becomes lexical retrieval; cause convenient substring matching; mitigation exact normalized equality only and hard refusal of later channels

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + fold_1 preserves continuation source and consumes only the published Slice2 proof
  + fold_2 separates exact proposal discovery from package authority and downstream execution
  + fold_3 models seeds gates contributions paths lattice boundary states proof and cursor
  + fold_4 checks every decision against available catalogue fabric and query fields
  + fold_5 prunes lexical learned provider attention persistence effect remote FPGA and Minecraft behavior
  + fold_6 adds ambiguity authorization lifecycle boundary root cursor cycle and clipping adversarial cases
  + fold_7 converges on one pure exact scanner one verifier and no downstream detail projection or provider integration
  + [gain_delta] Cantor can now turn signed semantic identity and exact terms into inspectable bounded candidates without an LLM or similarity heuristic
  + [exhaustion_state] phase_locked_for_Slice3_implementation

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty requires exact bases explicit ambiguity truthful missing-declaration guards and no score laundering
  + Security requires root equality read-only effect boundary authority scope lifecycle gates budgets and cursor freshness
  + Weaver proposes only exact binding and typed relation associations without final authority
  + Planner orders staged gates traversal lattice clipping continuation and stop conditions
  + Refiner retains canonical candidates and the smallest candidate-level proof while deferring detail projection
  + Scribe records original bases contributions decisions omissions paths source anchors and digest identity
  + Observer validates the whole input-output correspondence and refuses partial uncommitted state

& [Decision]
  + activate Slice3 pure exact scanner typed faults cursor and focused tests in a dependency-light cantor_core sibling module
  + allow no lexical embedding learned provider attention bridge persistence remote hidden-state effect FPGA or Minecraft implementation
  + require solution proof narrative file-change attribution full workspace verification lint format and evidence refresh before completion

